From 16c00f34c29e24ee1217c32cede486d90de4eb68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Mar 2026 11:28:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu: add Liverpool/Gladius SCLK force
 driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds liverpool_clk.c and liverpool_clk.h, a minimal one-shot SCLK
force for the PS4 Liverpool and Gladius GPUs.

After ps4-kexec performs a GFX soft-reset, the SCLK divider (DID)
reverts to the fuse-burnt startup value in GCK_SCLK_FUSES, leaving
the GPU at strap frequency (~200-300 MHz). pp_smu_ip_block is present
in the IP block list for CHIP_LIVERPOOL and CHIP_GLADIUS but produces
no functional DPM table and has never raised the clock across any
ps4-linux rebase. The GPU has been stuck at strap speed on every
kernel version shipped.

Uses the CG_SCLK_CNTL direct-control path (SCLKDIRCNTLEN +
SCLKDIRCNTLTOG) to force SCLKDIRCNTLDIVIDER = 1 (Ã·1, full SPLL
output) from cik_common_hw_init(). SCLKDIRCNTLEN is kept set
permanently to prevent any dormant DPM path from lowering the clock.

The SPLL VCO is not modified: a GFX soft-reset does not reconfigure
the GCK PLL block (separate power domain managed by SMC firmware).
The function logs SPLL PDIVA and FBDIV at init time and warns if
PDIVA > 4, indicating the SPLL may need separate reprogramming.

Register map sourced from bonaire.rai (GCK block, SMC indirect).
Thermal safety is maintained by the Aeolia/Belize/Baikal EMC which
independently enforces GPU kill at 72Â°C (ICC 0x0B/0x05 domain 2)
and APU shutdown at 97Â°C regardless of clock register state.

Signed-off-by: rmux <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
